Section: 4.3 Code switching and transliteration
Text: 4.3 Code switching and transliteration Code-switching (CS)—the mixing of multi- ple languages within a single utterance—and transliteration—writing that is not in the lan- guage’s standard script—present unique test cases for M-BERT, which is pre-trained on monolingual, standard-script corpora. Generalizing to code- switching is similar to other cross-lingual trans- fer scenarios, but would beneﬁt to an even larger degree from a shared multilingual representation.

